1
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:29,154
FROM ME TO YOU: KIMI NI TODOKE
3RD SEASON

2
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:26,002
- Good morning!
- It's been a while!

3
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,880
- How was summer break?
- I had way too much fun!

4
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:34,427
It's the start
of the second term.

5
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:37,097
And for a second-year, that means...

6
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,599
Our class trip's soon! Okinawa!

7
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:42,560
I can't wait. It's gonna be my first time.

8
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:45,063
- Yeah, same for me.
- Same here.

9
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,816
Gotta avoid the UV rays.

10
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:52,070
So, hey. When it's November here,
what month is it in Okinawa?

11
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:53,655
It's also November.

12
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:54,572
What?! No way!

13
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:57,242
Chizu, turn it down a notch, okay?

14
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:03,039
If I can't get pumped now,
then when am I allowed to, huh?

15
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:08,169
I'm so sorry about that.
Are you all right?

16
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,004
It's okay. I'm fine.

17
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:13,716
- What do you think you're doing?
- S-- s-- s-- sorry!

18
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:17,679
Come on. See that? Sawako's being calm.

19
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:21,266
She's not getting all carried away
like you over some silly field trip.

20
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:23,852
And you need to apologize to her too.

21
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:27,188
S-- sorry about that. You good?

22
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:28,231
Yay.

23
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:29,149
-"Yay"?
-"Yay"?

24
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,527
Don't worry, be happy!

25
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,779
She's so excited.

26
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,447
- Let's take pics.
- Mm?

27
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:38,867
A whole bunch.

28
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,414
Shall we go shopping
for our trip, then?

29
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:48,126
We'll be together the whole time!
Four nights and five days straight!

30
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:50,253
We will? Really?

31
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:52,088
Ahh!

32
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:54,007
Kazehaya too.

33
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:59,304
Oh! We're getting split into groups today
for the upcoming trip.

34
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:00,513
Mm-hmm.

35
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:03,766
They're both
still acting the same.

36
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,435
Oh, Kazehaya.

37
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:08,730
At least start calling Sawako
by her first name already.

38
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:09,647
Mmm. Mmm.

39
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:11,149
Heya!

40
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:14,986
When the two of you are alone, do you
call each other by your first names, or...

41
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:18,531
I-- I don't see
how that's any of your business.

42
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:21,117
Sure, I get it. It's just that
I've been hearing these rumors

43
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:23,286
that you've already
met each other's parents and stuff,

44
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:24,829
so I was just curious.

45
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,873
How the hell did you find out?

46
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:30,418
You know how well-connected
I am, right? It's easy for me.

47
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:33,171
Wow! They're already meeting the parents.

48
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,382
What's wrong
with all the people around us?

49
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:39,010
Every one of them's
so insensitive and rude.

50
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:45,600
Four nights and five days.

51
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:52,232
I've never gotten to spend
that much time with them before.

52
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:53,358
Another first.

53
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:59,405
EPISODE 2
SCHOOL TRIP

54
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:05,370
Cool. It looks like
we've figured out our groups, then.

55
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:06,788
Yeah.

56
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,001
Hey.

57
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:13,461
Hey.

58
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:16,673
You stopped coming by.

59
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:20,510
It's just because you're busy these days,
that's all.

60
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:21,886
With practice.

61
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:22,929
That's it?

62
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:24,639
Uh-huh.

63
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:31,187
Hm.

64
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:36,276
Since summer break,
everything just feels so awkward.

65
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:39,237
Everyone decide on a leader
for your group and report back.

66
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,991
- 'Kay!
- Leader? Should that be me, then? Or...

67
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,622
- I'll do it.
- Oh.

68
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:50,748
Huh? Really?

69
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:51,749
Awesome!

70
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:56,254
It's like you read my mind.

71
00:04:57,338 --> 00:05:01,384
Leaders, meet me after school.
And no skipping out on this, got it?

72
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,385
Huh?!

73
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,849
Can...

74
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:10,768
...I wait for... you?

75
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,147
Mmm.

76
00:05:17,191 --> 00:05:20,445
They really are
girlfriend and boyfriend, after all.

77
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,571
Mm.

78
00:05:29,662 --> 00:05:32,457
- I'm heading to the meeting now.
- O-- okay.

79
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:36,169
- Sawako.
- Huh?

80
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:39,047
While you're waiting for Kazehaya
to finish up his meeting,

81
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:42,300
how about the three of us decide on
what we wanna do during our free time?

82
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:43,509
Can we?!

83
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:47,180
I wanna eat some soki soba.

84
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:49,849
And then buy that... that something-dama.

85
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:51,017
The ball thingies.

86
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,770
Oh, churadama. Huh?

87
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:03,279
Y-- Yui and Andy! Was that a confession?!

88
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:04,739
N-- no idea.

89
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:14,749
- There are new couples everywhere.
- Uh-huh.

90
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:19,128
Happens this time of year.
During festivals or class trips.

91
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:24,092
- All hail the queen.
- Help us, Master Sawako.

92
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:26,177
N-- no, don't ask me! I'm useless!

93
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:32,225
Hey... you're not gonna
hang out alone with Ryu, are you?

94
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:33,142
Huh?

95
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:36,312
- Like, during our free time.
- What? I'm confused.

96
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:40,441
Well, see, if things end up
working out between Andy and Yui,

97
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:43,027
and they're dating,
then they'll hang out together.

98
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:43,945
Mmm.

99
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:47,824
And you're going to be spending
lots of time alone with Kazehaya.

100
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:53,496
So, then, if Chizu and Ryu end up
spending their time together,

101
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:57,458
that'll just leave me and Joe, which means
we're stuck hanging together by default!

102
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:00,586
Now, you're not planning
on getting together with Ryu, right?

103
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,839
N-- no, of course not!

104
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:05,007
She-- she's not?

105
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,427
What's up though?

106
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,762
Like, is there anything new
going on lately?

107
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:10,680
Uh?

108
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:21,232
What? There is something, isn't there?

109
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,109
I mean, there may be something!

110
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:24,277
Or... or not!

111
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,572
Yeah, nothing going on at all!
Nothing of interest ever happened!

112
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:30,116
- Why are you being so weird, then?
- I'm not weird!

113
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:32,160
Everything is normal!

114
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,082
Do you have anyone you're interested in?

115
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,834
No. Not at all.

116
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:42,837
I've never had a crush
on anyone except Toru.

117
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:48,843
It didn't work out, but still,
I'm glad I got to tell him how I felt.

118
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:52,180
I've been curious.
What did you say when you confessed?

119
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:55,683
I just... said, "I, uh, like you."

120
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,144
- Sawako?
- Huh?!

121
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:00,938
Well, I said, "I like you"?

122
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:05,568
- Interesting. It was that simple, huh?
- Huh?

123
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:08,946
Well, then, what kinds of things do you
say to people when you confess to them?

124
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:10,364
Uh...

125
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:14,160
I've never told anyone I like them.

126
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:15,411
Really?!

127
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:17,622
Nope. Never.

128
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:20,708
When you finally get the chance to do it,
it'll feel great!

129
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:24,086
Huh? I'm good. That's the guy's job.

130
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,380
Wha-- Well that sucks.

131
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:29,383
Don't you want
to have a boyfriend, Yano?

132
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:33,638
Yeah, I suppose I do.
Don't know who though.

133
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:36,599
Huh?
On the hunt for a new boyfriend, Ayane?

134
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:41,354
Well, you could put me in the running.
I'm totally available right now.

135
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:44,982
- Nah, I'm good.
- Wow, that was cold.

136
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,484
And how are you doin'?

137
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:50,446
You seem good. Like, really happy.

138
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:54,659
- Oh, master!
- Come on now! That's no good!

139
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:58,287
Tears don't suit you, Sadako.
Let's change that.

140
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:01,457
You're so stiff.

141
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:03,000
What is this?

142
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:07,255
So did that bother you?
I didn't know you were the jealous type.

143
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:08,673
Oh, shut up!

144
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:09,632
Jealous?!

145
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:11,676
- You seem like a generally chilled guy.
- Hold on.

146
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:15,680
How did we end up in a position
where Kento's walking home with us?

147
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:18,140
For real. He's got some mad skills.

148
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:26,691
I was wondering what size luggage
we should use for the trip? This big?

149
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:28,192
Thiiiis big!

150
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:31,153
We should bring
an umbrella with us too, right?

151
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:33,656
I'm going to ask
for a little allowance increase.

152
00:09:33,739 --> 00:09:35,324
They're inspecting our luggage.

153
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,410
I doubt Pin's gonna be strict.

154
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:39,120
Y-- Yano.

155
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:40,705
Uh?

156
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,792
- Do you think we could chat?
- Uh...

157
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:45,960
Wh-- what's up?

158
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,924
Hmm. Then, I guess I'll say it here.

159
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:54,260
- Here?!
- No way!

160
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:56,721
Uh, please go out with me!

161
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:58,931
Uh...

162
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:04,812
My name's Mogi. I'm from Class B.

163
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:08,065
Yano... you probably
don't know anything about me yet.

164
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:11,319
Do you remember
us bumping into each other?

165
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,363
- No.
- I figured.

166
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:18,826
But still, if you'd like...

167
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:22,830
Uh, we can take it slow.
Just start getting to know each other?

168
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:23,998
Okay.

169
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:25,875
Eh?

170
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:28,294
Let's go out.

171
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:30,796
Whaa!

172
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,010
Uh, we're going to be leaving
in just a bit.

173
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:39,680
Be sure to keep any valuables
you brought with you in your carry-on.

174
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:43,351
When you go through the security check,
please refrain from talking

175
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,186
and be as efficient as possible.

176
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:49,148
Once you've taken your seat on the plane,
be careful not to talk too loudly,

177
00:10:49,231 --> 00:10:51,651
I don't want you bothering
the people around you.

178
00:10:57,573 --> 00:10:59,283
-   We're flying!
- Finally.

179
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,452
- It's so cool!
- The day we've all waited for.

180
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:04,163
The start of our class trip!

181
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:08,459
- Sawa, snackies!
- Oh, thank you.

182
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:13,297
No, stop. Not like that.
Say, "Ah!" It's jerky!

183
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:17,218
- Ahh!
- Mmm!

184
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,929
But, anyways...

185
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:21,639
Check that out over there.

186
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,519
Like you said,

187
00:11:26,602 --> 00:11:30,272
people confessing their feelings
to each other happens a lot during trips.

188
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:33,901
Or someone
calls you out to "talk." Every time.

189
00:11:33,984 --> 00:11:36,612
Kuronuma. Here. You want one?

190
00:11:36,696 --> 00:11:38,406
Oh, thank you!

191
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:46,580
D-- did I do something wrong?
I messed up, didn't I?

192
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:48,165
N-- no.

193
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:50,501
I'm going to go to the bathroom now.

194
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:51,502
Me too.

195
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:58,050
So this is where you're sitting.

196
00:11:58,134 --> 00:11:59,593
Yeah. What about you?

197
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:00,928
Well, I'm over there.

198
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:04,557
- I can't wait for Okinawa.
- Yeah, same.

199
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,267
Right, I'll go first.

200
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:08,853
Looks like things
are going pretty well between them.

201
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,480
But it's kinda awkward.

202
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:15,276
I mean, this whole time, I sorta figured
Ayane and I would get together.

203
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:18,654
What? Well, good for them.
Whatever it takes.

204
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:19,822
Yeah, sure.

205
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,451
But still, there are other ways
it can happen!

206
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:27,329
Huh? What the heck, Kento?
What's he trying to say?

207
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:30,583
Yano's boyfriend is...
Mogi, right?

208
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:32,752
Are things going okay between them?

209
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,545
Yeah. Seems like it.

210
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:39,884
Are you going to
date him, Yano-chin?

211
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:43,471
Yeah.
He seems like a good guy, so why not?

212
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:47,767
Besides, the class trip
might be even more fun this way.

213
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,897
I... I think it will be fun.

214
00:12:58,652 --> 00:13:01,655
Yeah, it's going to be so much fun!

215
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,373
It's Okinawa!

216
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,584
Whoa!

217
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:18,255
Whoa, the humidity.
I feel like I could swim in this air.

218
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:21,509
There's no mistaking it.
We're not up north anymore!

219
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:30,518
We finally made it!
So what do we have after this?

220
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:33,771
We get a little time to rest,
have some dinner, and then bath time.

221
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:37,107
- We should go check out the hotel.
- Okay.

222
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,985
Oh, Sawako.
Did you bring the underwear we got?

223
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:43,072
Oh. Uh... yes, I did.

224
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,120
- Kazehaya!
- Uh... mm-hmm?

225
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:59,296
Ya know, us girls, we went shopping
the other day to buy panties.

226
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,798
Including Sawako.

227
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:06,136
- Uh... Uh... That's nice?
- Kazehaya, that's not all.

228
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:10,099
She got... side-tie ones.

229
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:13,853
Why would...

230
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,564
What am I supposed to do
with that information, huh?

231
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:18,023
Thanks for waiting.

232
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:21,318
- What's up? What was that all about?
- Nothing!

233
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,822
- You better not tell anyone else.
- I won't, obviously!

234
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:33,664
I've never seen you without a skirt on.

235
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:36,917
I wanted to wear something
easy to move around in,

236
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,252
since we'll be active.

237
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:41,672
- Does it look weird?
- No, not at all.

238
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,602
- You thinkin' about--
- No, I'm not!

239
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,812
Don't ask! And don't look!

240
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:03,027
Here's the thing
about panties, Sawako.

241
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,529
A woman doesn't wear them
just for herself.

242
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,864
It's just underwear.

243
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,283
Women wear them
to pump themselves up. That's all.

244
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:12,369
You only say that 'cause you've
not needed them in that way yet, Chizu.

245
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:13,746
What's that mean?!

246
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,248
What an adult conversation.

247
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,542
What about you, Yano-chin?
How's Mogi-cchi?

248
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:22,504
Oh, we're planning to meet each other
tomorrow evening.

249
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:26,342
Then we're planning to walk around
Kokusai-dori, just the two of us.

250
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:28,802
- Is that cool?
- Yeah, fine, go ahead.

251
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:31,263
Sawako, you should
hang out with Kazehaya.

252
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,474
Wha-- what about me?

253
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:34,975
Let's see...

254
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,229
You've got Ryu, right? And Joe.

255
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,190
I knew it!

256
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:43,734
I knew this would happen,
so I can't be upset!

257
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:44,902
But still!

258
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,820
- So, uh...
- Mmm?

259
00:15:47,446 --> 00:15:51,825
You two... would call this conversation
a heart-to-heart between girls,

260
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:52,785
wouldn't you?

261
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:56,872
- Of course.
- What's up? Did something happen?

262
00:15:57,539 --> 00:16:01,752
Uh, it's just, there's something
I wanted to ask you, Ayane.

263
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:05,881
What is it?
You can ask me anything you want.

264
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:08,008
I... I was wondering

265
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:12,888
when did you...
you first start having feelings for Mogi?

266
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:18,644
Huh?! Wait, do you mean
you started liking him?

267
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:19,728
Really? Like, when?!

268
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:25,734
Well... I wouldn't go
out of my way to tell everyone...

269
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,069
We're already dating.

270
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:29,571
You're always like this!
It's so frustrating!

271
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:31,281
You're so pushy with other people!

272
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:34,493
But then you pretty much
never talk about yourself!

273
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:37,621
I get it! Next time something happens,
I'll tell you.

274
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,082
- You mean it?
- Yes.

275
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:51,927
I want to drink something cold.
Oh, and fizzy too.

276
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:54,638
- I wonder what they have here?
- Tea for me.

277
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:56,640
- Oh.
- It's them.

278
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:58,892
Oh.

279
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:02,104
What's up? You just finish your bath too?

280
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:04,898
Your hair, Ryu. Sea urchin.

281
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,942
That's not true. Sheesh.

282
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,903
- Hmm?
- Mm?

283
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:13,198
Huh?! But what if I wanna
choose my own drink?!

284
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:15,409
Then, go right ahead. Pick one.

285
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,911
Let's see...

286
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:22,875
Um, how about... I go with a... Maybe?

287
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:29,298
This one.

288
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:32,384
You can buy some ice cream
for me as payback.

289
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,553
Huh?! That's way more expensive!

290
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:39,016
What would you like?

291
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:40,893
A Jasmine tea sounds good to me.

292
00:17:41,268 --> 00:17:42,686
OKINAWAN JASMINE TEA

293
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:46,315
As soon as I find my wallet...

294
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:49,818
- I remember this happening before.
- Huh?

295
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:53,405
Huh?! The coffee!

296
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:58,452
Here. This one's on me.

297
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,413
This isn't my normal routine.

298
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:06,919
I'm living my life outside of school.
But Kazehaya is here.

299
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:10,839
Thank you for that.

300
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:18,555
How nice! Did he say, "free"?

301
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:21,975
Tell me where I can get some of that
free jasmine tea for myself.

302
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,811
You're a menace
to society, Yano.

303
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:29,191
So how far have you gone with Sadako?
Give me the deets!

304
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:32,277
You must've kissed by now
or at least you held hands?

305
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:34,571
- Shut up.
- You suck! Bleurgh!

306
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,032
- Huh?
- Uh-oh.

307
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:40,244
Is the teacher here to check in on us?
I'll get it.

308
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:43,372
You'd call us friends,
wouldn't you, Ryu?

309
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:44,373
Sure.

310
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:48,460
Ha! So, yeah, what do you
and Sadako do on your dates anyway?

311
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:51,171
- Dude, leave me alone!
- Ryu?

312
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:53,966
- Huh?
- It's a girl from Class C.

313
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,467
Huh?

314
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,441
Rise and shine!

315
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:20,075
- Huh!
- That's right! We're on
the class trip right now, aren't we? Huh?

316
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:22,786
- I'm getting your wake-up face!
- Wha-- what?

317
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:25,664
- Oooh! Yeah! Nice!
- How are you so loud?

318
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,167
- Your turn now!
- Knock it off.

319
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:32,337
Wow! I woke up inside a hotel.

320
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:37,426
And my friends' faces
were the very first thing I saw.

321
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,429
I get to eat breakfast with everyone!

322
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:47,019
And the person I like is here.

323
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:48,937
G'morning!

324
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,522
Good morning.

325
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:52,608
So did you sleep okay?

326
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:55,444
Honestly, I was too excited to sleep.

327
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:59,948
Things like this
don't usually happen to me.

328
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:02,534
Same for me. Everyone kept talking.

329
00:20:03,076 --> 00:20:04,786
Joe was more annoying than usual.

330
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,955
That's just him. Always.

331
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,332
What a surprise.

332
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:18,342
I'm your tour guide, Higa.
I'm so glad you're all here with me today.

333
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:21,178
Boom! Kyu! Bang!

334
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:24,640
The pleasure is all mine.

335
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,225
For real?

336
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:29,102
-   Well, this'll be a ride.
- How friendly.

337
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:36,235
Group photo time! Over here!

338
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:42,699
This way.

339
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:48,455
- Did you hear what he said?
-"This way"!

340
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:49,957
That was so good!

341
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:52,334
Come stand where you belong. With me!

342
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:55,587
- You are so annoying!
- Come on. Go ahead.

343
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:10,978
All right, everyone!
Look over here for me, okay?

344
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:14,898
I've never taken a group photo

345
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:17,067
quite like this.

346
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,410
Make sure you all stay with your groups!

347
00:21:26,493 --> 00:21:28,787
And meet back at the bus on time!

348
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:34,668
Care to see the manatees with me?

349
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:36,712
Oh, I've seen them. Many times.

350
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:47,514
Pretty!

351
00:21:48,181 --> 00:21:50,392
That shrimp is huge!

352
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:53,854
- Wow, there's so many.
- Mm-hmm.

353
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:56,440
Hmm?

354
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:06,992
Kuronuma.

355
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:10,787
Right there. Look, there's a whale shark.

356
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:30,849
- Oh! D-- did you take one?
- Mm-hmm.

357
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:34,853
Oh! It's coming over here. Okay, smile!

358
00:22:34,936 --> 00:22:39,232
What is going on?

359
00:22:39,316 --> 00:22:41,360
I'm not used to posing for photos.

360
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:45,864
And, if I think about it,
Kazehaya's in some of these.

361
00:22:45,947 --> 00:22:49,409
But only in the background
or corner of some of the group pictures.

362
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:51,995
I haven't actually
taken any of just him yet.

363
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:54,373
I'm so nervous.

364
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:57,876
M-- maybe I should try it now?

365
00:23:00,962 --> 00:23:02,255
You looked over at me!

366
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:04,508
- Obviously.
- Y-- yeah, you're right.

367
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:06,927
Yay!

368
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:23,360
That manta ray just now
looked exactly like me!

369
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:26,822
So awesome!
It's the bottom!

370
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,365
It's huge!

371
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,576
I'm so happy.

372
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:34,871
I've made so many new memories.

373
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,565
Truly happy.

374
00:24:13,368 --> 00:24:17,247
The aquarium is the bomb!
It's so much fun!

375
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:21,585
- I took tons of photos too.
- Oh! Yay! Let me see 'em!

376
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:24,087
Look at Joe's face! Idiot!

377
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:28,258
- Do you wanna see ours too?
- Yeah. Show me.

378
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:37,893
There are... so many of me.

379
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:43,315
These are everyone's memories...
and I'm there too.

380
00:24:47,944 --> 00:24:50,739
Wow! It really does
look like an elephant!

381
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:52,407
You're right.

382
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:02,000
The ocean sure is beautiful.

383
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:07,547
Yano?!

384
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:10,717
Wha-- what are you doing
standing out here holding a parasol?!

385
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:14,304
You're so damn loud.
I'm protecting my skin from UV rays.

386
00:25:14,387 --> 00:25:17,432
Why? Did you come all the way
to Okinawa just to pick up girls?

387
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:24,940
There was the aquarium, right?
And the pineapples...

388
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:27,442
And then chillin'
at the hotel's private beach!

389
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:30,445
But today was the day
we were looking forward to the most!

390
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:31,404
Hold on.

391
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:35,575
So, that means we're almost done, then?
Like, it's all downhill from here?

392
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:38,912
Either way, I can't wait
until our free time tonight.

393
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:40,497
The beach and the stars!

394
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:44,167
Speaking of, I promised Mogi-cchi
I'd meet up with him there.

395
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:46,378
Oh yeah? How naughty of you!

396
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:47,671
In what way?

397
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:51,675
No, thank you! Give up!

398
00:25:51,758 --> 00:25:52,968
Leave me alone!

399
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:55,095
Even when you're angry, you're so cute!

400
00:25:55,178 --> 00:25:56,680
Stop following me!

401
00:25:57,806 --> 00:26:00,684
I was on my way to the beach too!
What a coincidence!

402
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:05,230
- I'm not going anymore!
- - No, wait!
- You run so fast!

403
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:08,483
K-- Kurumi? What was that?

404
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:12,028
Well, according to my research,
Ume's current reputation is

405
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:14,114
"the girl who gives it to you straight."

406
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:16,616
She's been gathering
quite the following too.

407
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:18,493
I'm confused but impressed.

408
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,499
Seriously though,
Kurumi really is popular.

409
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:26,960
Chigusa found out that
eight people in our class

410
00:26:27,043 --> 00:26:28,003
have been confessed to.

411
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:30,338
Amazing. She's not even
in our class anymore.

412
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:32,507
Wait. Does that include me?

413
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:35,510
Oh yeah, probably.
Guess that makes nine, then.

414
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:38,430
- Huh?
- What are you talking about?

415
00:26:38,513 --> 00:26:42,225
You're forgetting to include your
childhood friend in that list of yours!

416
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:45,228
Ryu! Someone confessed to him yesterday!

417
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:46,813
Huh?

418
00:26:50,150 --> 00:26:51,943
But, what? Is that true?

419
00:26:52,027 --> 00:26:55,155
- He also rejected her on the spot.
- What?

420
00:26:55,238 --> 00:26:57,365
The whole thing
went down last night.

421
00:26:57,449 --> 00:27:00,118
She came to our room
and asked to talk to him.

422
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:07,250
So that's how it is.
He doesn't want to tell me about it.

423
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:13,381
I see. He said no... of course.

424
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:16,384
My eyes are only for Chizuru.

425
00:27:17,552 --> 00:27:18,595
It's a secret.

426
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:28,605
The ocean's
completely different down here.

427
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:29,856
Y-- yeah.

428
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:32,442
The sand is so white,
and the water's so blue.

429
00:27:32,525 --> 00:27:33,360
Right?

430
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:39,491
Now, Kazehaya,
please take care of Sawako.

431
00:27:39,574 --> 00:27:41,785
Good care, good care--

432
00:27:41,868 --> 00:27:44,496
Now, remember,
to conduct yourself with propriety.

433
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:47,082
You're still children
who can't support yourselves.

434
00:27:47,165 --> 00:27:49,417
And children
should interact like children.

435
00:27:51,336 --> 00:27:53,338
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

436
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:55,215
Yeah, I know that, okay?!

437
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:56,841
Oh, I, uh... I'm sorry!

438
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:59,177
Uh, n-- no,
I-- I didn't mean you.

439
00:27:59,678 --> 00:28:01,012
What did I just see?

440
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:02,597
Aw, cute!

441
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:05,433
- Uh, Kento?
- What's up?

442
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:06,976
Ah, Yano!

443
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:10,438
- Are you still free tonight?
- Yeah.

444
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:12,565
Later.

445
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:17,612
- Where's a good place to meet up?
- Oh, uh, where we said before.

446
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,990
- Sure. See you later.
- See ya.

447
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,452
- Awesome, man.
- Good job!

448
00:28:51,187 --> 00:28:52,981
- Good night.
- Mm-hmm.

449
00:29:06,494 --> 00:29:07,495
What are you doing?

450
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:10,957
It's time to go to sleep now.
Back to your room.

451
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:14,127
Oh, it's just you scared me.

452
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:18,006
What's that supposed to mean?
I'm your homeroom teacher, remember?

453
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:19,215
So what about it?

454
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:22,385
You were supposed to be our chaperone,
but you just came here to flirt!

455
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:23,970
That's none of your business!

456
00:29:24,053 --> 00:29:27,098
What does it matter
to you anyway?

457
00:29:27,182 --> 00:29:31,478
To think this world's filled
with these poor excuses for men.

458
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:35,398
- So, hey.
- Huh?

459
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:38,401
Have you been in love before?

460
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:45,241
Random. Well, yeah.

461
00:29:50,413 --> 00:29:51,247
Uh...

462
00:29:56,127 --> 00:29:57,587
So what's wrong with her?

463
00:30:21,444 --> 00:30:23,196
Y-- you k-- kissed?!

464
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:25,365
Chill out. You asked me how things went.

465
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:28,785
- So I gave you the rundown.
- They kissed! No wonder they took so long!

466
00:30:28,868 --> 00:30:30,870
I knew it!
I had a feeling something was up!

467
00:30:30,954 --> 00:30:33,623
Calm down! Seriously.

468
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:37,377
K-- kissing?

469
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:40,338
They did that?!

470
00:30:41,798 --> 00:30:43,383
H-- how grown up!

471
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:46,719
Now what?

472
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:48,972
Oh, it's, uh... nothing.

473
00:30:49,055 --> 00:30:52,475
I'll say this now.
That you're going to do it too, Sawako!

474
00:30:57,188 --> 00:30:59,190
N-- no way!

475
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:00,441
Huh? You won't?

476
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:02,694
- Yes, you will!
- I... I will?!

477
00:31:02,777 --> 00:31:04,487
You're absolutely
going to kiss him!

478
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:06,197
I... I am?!

479
00:31:06,281 --> 00:31:09,409
- Or maybe not.
- I... I'm not?!

480
00:31:09,492 --> 00:31:10,451
Which one is it?

481
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:13,913
Shota, are you sick?

482
00:31:13,997 --> 00:31:15,665
I... don't think...

483
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:27,260
Won't my... heart explode?

484
00:31:30,597 --> 00:31:31,764
It won't.

485
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:35,393
Lucky! It's not fair!

486
00:31:35,476 --> 00:31:38,521
Oh yeah,
when I was gone, what did you guys do?

487
00:31:38,605 --> 00:31:40,148
Go visit Kazehaya and Ryu?

488
00:31:40,231 --> 00:31:43,276
Huh? Why would we do that?
We just had a girls' hang!

489
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,280
A kiss?

490
00:31:59,125 --> 00:32:01,044
J... just a dream!

491
00:32:01,669 --> 00:32:03,713
What's wrong?

492
00:32:03,796 --> 00:32:06,049
- Ah, shut up!
- N-- nothing!

493
00:32:06,132 --> 00:32:08,217
- What time is it?
- I'm totally fine!

494
00:32:08,301 --> 00:32:11,763
- What's going on?
- D-- don't worry!

495
00:32:13,556 --> 00:32:16,434
Everyone! Let's take a photo, okay?

496
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:18,686
Say cheese!

497
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:22,941
What d'you think?
Which class sounds good?

498
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:25,109
- Hmm, lemme think.
- It's hard.

499
00:32:25,193 --> 00:32:28,613
Okay. How about we say what
we wanna do out loud at the same time?

500
00:32:28,696 --> 00:32:29,697
Yeah, good idea.

501
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:32,367
Hey, Joe, check it out.
They're sure having fun.

502
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:34,619
- Totally! Even Sadako!
- One, two...

503
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:36,079
- Sanshin!
- Ceramics!

504
00:32:36,162 --> 00:32:37,372
HUH?

505
00:32:38,164 --> 00:32:39,999
'Kay, Sawako, have fun with that.

506
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:41,834
We're going to do sanshin.

507
00:32:43,503 --> 00:32:46,005
No, actually, I want to do sanshin too!

508
00:32:46,089 --> 00:32:48,716
No, you should go
and do your ceramics painting.

509
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:52,303
We came all the way to Okinawa, after all.
We should all do what we want.

510
00:32:52,387 --> 00:32:55,682
Yeah, but what I want to do is keep
having fun with whatever you're doing!

511
00:32:55,765 --> 00:32:57,684
You should be
having fun with that.

512
00:32:58,476 --> 00:32:59,686
Hmm?

513
00:32:59,769 --> 00:33:02,772
- Wha-- No, I can't!
- Huh?

514
00:33:03,439 --> 00:33:05,149
Oh, she says that she can't.

515
00:33:05,233 --> 00:33:07,026
No, but that's not what I meant to say!

516
00:33:09,612 --> 00:33:12,532
- Okay, but you know what? I...
- Did they team up?

517
00:33:14,575 --> 00:33:17,954
I... I can't stop thinking about
that dream I had!

518
00:33:18,037 --> 00:33:19,539
By the way, Kuronuma,

519
00:33:19,622 --> 00:33:22,667
I remember you telling my dad before
that you like drawing and stuff.

520
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:25,670
So do you draw often?

521
00:33:25,753 --> 00:33:27,714
No, it's just a casual hobby.

522
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:29,966
I'm not particularly
good at it or anything.

523
00:33:30,049 --> 00:33:31,300
Huh? Show me.

524
00:33:31,968 --> 00:33:34,554
Next time, maybe I'll ask you to draw me.

525
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:36,764
KAZEHAYA-KUN

526
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:39,434
You're getting souvenirs
for your parents, right?

527
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:41,853
- Have you decided what yet?
- Y-- yeah.

528
00:33:41,936 --> 00:33:44,022
I'm buying some snow salt for my mom.

529
00:33:44,105 --> 00:33:47,191
Maybe a few other things
if I find something I know they'll like.

530
00:33:47,275 --> 00:33:50,987
I was thinking of getting one of those
Hawaiian-print shirts for my dad.

531
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:52,697
That's so him!

532
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:55,950
That kind of shirt would look good
on your dad too, don't you think?

533
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:57,952
Maybe you could get him one as well.

534
00:33:58,036 --> 00:34:00,246
Uh... then maybe I'll buy one

535
00:34:00,329 --> 00:34:02,749
that matches the one you're getting
for your dad?

536
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:04,208
Why would you do that?

537
00:34:05,835 --> 00:34:06,669
I'm done.

538
00:34:07,253 --> 00:34:10,298
Mine's kind of sloppy,
but I think it fits my vibe.

539
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:11,632
You think I could see it?

540
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:15,636
He's good!

541
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:18,139
How's yours going?
You're being so careful.

542
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:19,057
Uh...

543
00:34:22,643 --> 00:34:26,689
For some reason,
it ended up looking like Mr. Arai.

544
00:34:26,773 --> 00:34:28,900
OKINAWA'S DISTILLED ALCOHOL DRINK
AWAMORI

545
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:31,986
Ga-haa!

546
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,405
Wish we could just leave
that thing in Okinawa.

547
00:34:38,451 --> 00:34:41,621
Are you really sure it's okay
if I keep this for myself?

548
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:44,582
Yeah. You gave me yours, so we're even.

549
00:34:44,665 --> 00:34:46,876
I... I wonder if I should have.

550
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:49,837
I mean, it's kind of an abomination.

551
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:52,131
No, I'm glad. I'll put it on display.

552
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:55,343
It was an awesome memory.

553
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,517
- Oh.
- Fortunes?

554
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,102
FORTUNE

555
00:35:04,185 --> 00:35:06,270
GREAT BLESSING

556
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:07,980
"Great blessing"?!

557
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:09,941
Wow! That's so awesome.

558
00:35:10,691 --> 00:35:12,401
And I got "middle."

559
00:35:12,485 --> 00:35:14,612
"You will be released
from your previous suffering,

560
00:35:14,695 --> 00:35:16,656
and your luck is going to improve."

561
00:35:16,739 --> 00:35:17,740
You think it's true?

562
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:22,745
"Romance. What you're worried about
will be resolved soon."

563
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:25,081
"And your love will continue growing."

564
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:26,749
So it says.

565
00:35:28,376 --> 00:35:31,295
"Love... will continue growing."

566
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:41,097
"Choose someone you deeply respect,
and tell them you love them. Promising."

567
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:47,061
I wonder when it started?

568
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:51,357
In the summer, there was still space
between us when we walked.

569
00:35:53,192 --> 00:35:57,363
But now, we're so close
we sometimes bump into each other.

570
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:03,411
- Oh, there they are! Sawa!
- Where's Ryu and the guys?

571
00:36:04,036 --> 00:36:06,330
They all went over there
to check out the goats.

572
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:09,333
- Ah. I'll go say hi.
- Okay.

573
00:36:12,587 --> 00:36:15,506
- Oh, by the way, we got some goat milk.
- It's goat milk?

574
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:17,633
Stronger than a cow's, but good!

575
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:19,844
It's what they drink
in Heidi, Girl of the Alps.

576
00:36:20,428 --> 00:36:21,554
Y-- Yoshida.

577
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:24,307
- Oh.
- Mmm?

578
00:36:28,060 --> 00:36:28,895
Huh?

579
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:33,733
I... I was wondering
how you felt about Sanada?

580
00:36:37,653 --> 00:36:38,529
Oh yeah?

581
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:41,449
Say what you want directly.

582
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:44,577
You're not even being
straight up with me right now.

583
00:36:44,660 --> 00:36:47,330
So you're just gonna ask me
some vague question first?

584
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:51,417
That doesn't make any sense.
What do you really want?

585
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:54,921
Chizu's in full-on battle mode right now.
Just watch.

586
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:57,924
We're witnessing the other side
of the lovable goofball we know.

587
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:01,761
- I told him I like him.
- So?

588
00:37:01,844 --> 00:37:04,472
- But I was rejected.
- So?

589
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:07,975
Then I asked him
if there's someone else he likes.

590
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:10,061
There... was.

591
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:17,318
My first thought was
that maybe it was you,

592
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:19,487
since you two are always together.

593
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:20,488
So?

594
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:21,739
What if it is me?

595
00:37:21,822 --> 00:37:23,616
- Why would that matter to you?
- Huh?

596
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:26,827
Tell me. Why'd you bring all your friends?

597
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:28,537
Why are you asking me all this?

598
00:37:28,621 --> 00:37:30,206
What is the point here?

599
00:37:30,289 --> 00:37:33,292
What reaction could I possibly give you
that would make you happy?!

600
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:35,086
Uh, hold on, Chizu.

601
00:37:35,169 --> 00:37:36,504
So mean.

602
00:37:36,587 --> 00:37:38,798
It's just that, if you don't like Sanada,

603
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:42,134
I wanted to let him know
he shouldn't hang out with you so much.

604
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:46,347
That's none of your business!
You've no right to say anything!

605
00:37:51,644 --> 00:37:53,729
- S... Sae!
- So mean!

606
00:37:54,313 --> 00:37:55,898
Ch... Chizu.

607
00:37:57,650 --> 00:38:00,903
- Huh? What's wrong?
- Tell me!

608
00:38:00,987 --> 00:38:02,405
- Hey!
- Shut up!

609
00:38:03,614 --> 00:38:07,827
What did I do now?!
She's pissed!

610
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:09,829
It's not my fault, I swear,
but she's big mad!

611
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:23,092
All right.
I have plans to meet up with someone.

612
00:38:23,175 --> 00:38:24,343
Be back later.

613
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:26,721
'Kay. See you later.

614
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:37,773
- Sorry, Sawa.
- Huh?

615
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:39,942
Is it cool if I leave early too?

616
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:42,111
I could actually use some fresh air.

617
00:38:42,194 --> 00:38:43,571
Uh, of course.

618
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:46,615
Don't worry about me.
Just finish drying your hair, okay?

619
00:38:47,199 --> 00:38:48,784
Uh... thank you!

620
00:38:56,417 --> 00:38:59,670
- Taco rice is a different kind of taco.
- It's not octopus?

621
00:39:00,296 --> 00:39:02,048
- Ayane!
- Uh?

622
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:03,299
Well, let's eat!

623
00:39:03,382 --> 00:39:06,177
- What's up? You waiting for someone?
- Uh, yeah.

624
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,846
How nice.
Sure makes me wish I had a girlfriend.

625
00:39:08,929 --> 00:39:11,932
It looks like you have
tons of girlfriends to have fun with.

626
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:14,894
Those are friends.
But what I'm looking for is a lover.

627
00:39:14,977 --> 00:39:15,811
Gotcha.

628
00:39:16,937 --> 00:39:18,939
What's Mogi-cchi like anyway?

629
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:21,609
What kinds of things
do the two of you talk about?

630
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:23,194
What do we talk about?

631
00:39:26,238 --> 00:39:29,033
How's that information
any of your business whatsoever?

632
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:30,368
I just wanted some tea.

633
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:32,828
But I'm happy for you.

634
00:39:38,793 --> 00:39:39,794
Did you wait long?

635
00:39:40,628 --> 00:39:44,090
- No.
- And your friends, are they cool?

636
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:45,049
Yeah.

637
00:40:00,981 --> 00:40:02,066
Sorry.

638
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:14,245
- Hmm!
- What's with you?

639
00:40:15,162 --> 00:40:17,164
You've been acting weird.

640
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:22,795
I heard a girl told you she liked you
and that you rejected her!

641
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:25,005
But you didn't tell me anything about it!

642
00:40:26,715 --> 00:40:27,550
Why would I?

643
00:40:28,634 --> 00:40:31,345
It's none of your business.

644
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:34,056
Then don't send her right to me
so it's my problem!

645
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:36,100
Work it out with her,
and deal with it on your own!

646
00:40:36,183 --> 00:40:39,103
She rapid-fired
a whole lot of nonsense at me too!

647
00:40:39,728 --> 00:40:41,856
Y'know, that there's someone you like.

648
00:40:46,902 --> 00:40:47,987
You wanna know?

649
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:55,494
No, thanks. It's none of my business.

650
00:41:03,127 --> 00:41:05,754
Ayane forgot to bring her phone with her.

651
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:08,507
I'm glad I happened to find it
before I left the bath.

652
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:12,136
I wonder if the two of them
are back in our room by now?

653
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:17,725
Chizu looked kind of sad when she left.
She tried to hide it though.

654
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:21,395
Oh, right.
I should go buy some shikuwasa juice.

655
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,440
Oh.

656
00:41:25,274 --> 00:41:27,693
Did you just finish up
with your bath as well?

657
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:31,405
Oh, that's a coincidence.
I was the last one out of the girls'.

658
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:34,450
- Huh? Where's everyone else?
- Uh.

659
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:36,869
It wasn't a coincidence.

660
00:41:36,952 --> 00:41:39,413
I've been waiting for you.

661
00:41:39,997 --> 00:41:41,999
I waited for a while,
but you didn't show up.

662
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:44,793
So I thought that maybe
you already went back to your room.

663
00:41:44,877 --> 00:41:47,796
In fact, I was getting ready to leave,
but then I saw you.

664
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:52,718
- Oh! I'm sorry I made you wait.
- Don't be. It's okay.

665
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:55,971
It's fine.

666
00:41:57,264 --> 00:41:58,474
I just...

667
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:03,604
wanted to see you for a little bit...
so I'm glad.

668
00:42:09,109 --> 00:42:10,319
Uh...

669
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:12,905
I got my wish.

670
00:42:27,878 --> 00:42:30,005
I sat down so close to him

671
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:33,008
that if one of us moved at all,
we'd bump into each other.

672
00:42:34,093 --> 00:42:36,512
If I were to... look at his face...

673
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:43,018
my heart might actually explode.

674
00:42:48,607 --> 00:42:50,025
What do I do?

675
00:42:52,111 --> 00:42:54,947
I... can't look away.

676
00:42:56,782 --> 00:42:58,576
His body feels warm.

677
00:42:59,243 --> 00:43:03,080
I've never heard a sound like this
come out of me before.

678
00:43:04,748 --> 00:43:07,084
Not even a millimeter.

679
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:19,930
Hey. Close your eyes.

680
00:43:42,911 --> 00:43:46,749
I... I'm sorry.
I forgot my phone and just realized.

681
00:43:46,832 --> 00:43:50,252
Y-- your phone?!
I-- I-- I have it here with me!

682
00:43:50,336 --> 00:43:53,672
- J-- just give me a sec to find it!
- Uh... Oh, really? I'm sorry.

683
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:55,924
P-- please don't worry about it at all!

684
00:43:56,008 --> 00:43:58,344
- Here!
- Oh, uh, okay, thanks.

685
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:02,014
Cool. Continue.

686
00:44:03,390 --> 00:44:05,893
Contin--

687
00:44:05,976 --> 00:44:07,311
- Sorry!
- Uh?

688
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:11,607
Man... it's time for bed.

689
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:14,318
Y-- yeah.

690
00:44:15,402 --> 00:44:16,779
Sorry, Kuronuma.

691
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:21,200
See you tomorrow.

692
00:44:24,453 --> 00:44:25,371
It's okay.

693
00:44:26,372 --> 00:44:27,581
I won't tell anybody.

694
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:41,011
Just now,
if Ayane hadn't come when she did...

695
00:44:46,725 --> 00:44:48,352
I'm sorry, Sawako.

696
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:51,814
No, please. It's okay, really it is.

697
00:44:53,273 --> 00:44:54,316
Honest.

698
00:44:57,653 --> 00:45:01,448
Yeah, so anyway, did you go see him?

699
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:02,574
I mean Mogi.

700
00:45:02,658 --> 00:45:06,161
Yeah. And then I noticed
I didn't have my phone.

701
00:45:06,245 --> 00:45:07,663
Ah. Gotcha.

702
00:45:07,746 --> 00:45:10,332
Mmm. Makes sense. Yeah.

703
00:45:15,462 --> 00:45:17,089
I can still remember...

704
00:45:19,258 --> 00:45:20,843
the way he feels.

705
00:45:26,598 --> 00:45:28,016
Sorry.

706
00:45:29,768 --> 00:45:30,602
Mm-hmm

707
00:45:31,645 --> 00:45:32,604
Me too.

708
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:36,650
I've been kinda worried
about my friend,

709
00:45:36,734 --> 00:45:38,610
so I'm gonna head back early tonight.

710
00:45:38,694 --> 00:45:42,239
Oh. Okay.
We'll meet for tomorrow's free time, then.

711
00:45:42,322 --> 00:45:46,660
Oh, my phone's missing.
Is it in the changing room?

712
00:45:46,744 --> 00:45:47,953
Huh? Really?

713
00:45:48,537 --> 00:45:51,248
But... what if it really is gone?

714
00:45:51,331 --> 00:45:53,083
How am I supposed to get a hold of you?

715
00:45:57,087 --> 00:45:58,464
I'll figure it out.

716
00:46:12,311 --> 00:46:13,479
Huh? It's dark.

717
00:46:28,202 --> 00:46:29,161
Uh?

718
00:46:31,246 --> 00:46:33,457
Why are you sitting in the dark like this?

719
00:46:33,540 --> 00:46:36,627
- I'm turning the lights on.
- 'Kay. And welcome back.

720
00:46:40,214 --> 00:46:42,591
- That's interesting.
- Huh?

721
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:46,887
I thought you hated drinks
that were all sweet and sugary.

722
00:46:46,970 --> 00:46:49,389
SUPER SWEET

723
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:51,517
Yeah, I do!

724
00:46:51,600 --> 00:46:52,893
Huh? Seriously?

725
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:57,648
Maybe... it would have been
better if I stayed with her.

726
00:46:58,857 --> 00:47:01,902
I could tell
she was feeling sad from the start.

727
00:47:01,985 --> 00:47:06,323
But... I couldn't think
of anyone but myself.

728
00:47:06,406 --> 00:47:07,825
What's wrong with me?

729
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:13,455
- Chizu.
- Mmm?

730
00:47:14,998 --> 00:47:15,916
Take this.

731
00:47:18,460 --> 00:47:19,628
SHIKWASA JUICE

732
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:20,546
Thank you.

733
00:47:23,423 --> 00:47:24,341
What's the matter?

734
00:47:24,424 --> 00:47:26,093
Something happen?

735
00:47:26,176 --> 00:47:27,469
Uh...

736
00:47:30,472 --> 00:47:32,641
So the free time
we have on the fourth day,

737
00:47:32,724 --> 00:47:34,393
we're spending that with our boyfriends.

738
00:47:34,476 --> 00:47:37,896
- What about me?!
- Chizu, you've got Ryu.

739
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:42,860
No.

740
00:47:43,986 --> 00:47:44,820
It's nothing.

741
00:48:00,836 --> 00:48:01,670
Hey.

742
00:48:02,838 --> 00:48:06,133
So that's where you were.
Where are Joe and Andy?

743
00:48:06,216 --> 00:48:09,636
Um... they said they were gonna
visit the girls for a little bit.

744
00:48:10,679 --> 00:48:11,555
I see.

745
00:48:12,180 --> 00:48:13,015
Uh...

746
00:48:14,683 --> 00:48:16,143
is something wrong?

747
00:48:16,643 --> 00:48:19,563
Not really. What about you though, Ryu?

748
00:48:20,355 --> 00:48:23,191
Even if I told you,
it's not gonna change anything.

749
00:48:23,275 --> 00:48:24,109
It's not that.

750
00:48:24,693 --> 00:48:27,321
You don't usually drink those, right?
The sweet ones?

751
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:31,658
SUPER SWEET
MADE WITH WASANBON SUGAR

752
00:48:32,618 --> 00:48:34,369
I thought I was drinking water.

753
00:48:34,453 --> 00:48:35,579
Seriously?

754
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:43,086
I was being so careful.

755
00:48:50,010 --> 00:48:51,803
I totally lost control.

756
00:48:56,350 --> 00:48:59,770
Somehow,
it all feels like a dream.

757
00:49:02,397 --> 00:49:05,567
Did that actually happen in real life?

758
00:49:08,654 --> 00:49:12,240
But, the feelings are still with me.

759
00:49:13,659 --> 00:49:17,871
And tomorrow...
how am I supposed to face him?

760
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:26,421
There aren't any activities
planned for today.

761
00:49:26,505 --> 00:49:28,882
Just don't cause trouble for anyone.

762
00:49:30,425 --> 00:49:32,803
If you get lost, then contact us.

763
00:49:33,303 --> 00:49:34,346
That's it.

764
00:49:34,429 --> 00:49:35,931
Get outta here!

765
00:49:38,517 --> 00:49:41,019
Where should we go?
What should we do? Huh?

766
00:49:41,103 --> 00:49:43,647
- Hey! And tell me! What's out there?
- All right. Let's go.

767
00:49:43,730 --> 00:49:45,440
Bye.

768
00:49:47,901 --> 00:49:49,611
Last night, before I feel asleep...

769
00:49:49,695 --> 00:49:52,197
...I did a lot of thinking.

770
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:56,326
Hey, Chizu. If things are feeling
too awkward between you and Sanada,

771
00:49:56,410 --> 00:49:59,246
then how about you spend your free time
with us tomorrow?

772
00:49:59,329 --> 00:50:01,206
That's fine with me.

773
00:50:01,289 --> 00:50:03,750
I'll just have to skip
hanging out with Mogi-cchi.

774
00:50:03,834 --> 00:50:06,503
I am super disappointed about it though.

775
00:50:06,586 --> 00:50:07,462
Huh!

776
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:11,383
I can't do that.
Ayane will change her plans too.

777
00:50:11,466 --> 00:50:14,094
She's too considerate.
I don't wanna make her do that!

778
00:50:14,928 --> 00:50:16,805
Oh! What should I do?

779
00:50:18,098 --> 00:50:20,851
If it's too awkward,
spend your free time with me.

780
00:50:22,185 --> 00:50:24,271
Are you purposely avoiding me now?

781
00:50:24,354 --> 00:50:29,192
- Huh?! No! I'm not, at all!
- Gotcha. Never mind. It's fine.

782
00:50:30,444 --> 00:50:31,319
My bad.

783
00:50:32,404 --> 00:50:34,239
Sorry, Kuronuma.

784
00:50:40,287 --> 00:50:41,955
I ended up overthinking.

785
00:50:42,539 --> 00:50:45,375
And I wasn't able
to say anything to Chizu at all!

786
00:50:45,459 --> 00:50:48,462
Uh-- Should... we go?

787
00:50:48,545 --> 00:50:50,922
Uh, y-- yeah

788
00:50:55,635 --> 00:50:58,305
Huh? What's wrong with you two?

789
00:50:58,388 --> 00:51:01,058
You look like you're trying
to do the damn robot or something.

790
00:51:01,141 --> 00:51:03,560
Wha-- No. What are you talking about?!

791
00:51:03,643 --> 00:51:06,188
Well, it doesn't matter to me. Whatever!

792
00:51:06,271 --> 00:51:08,315
Here's the thing. Listen.

793
00:51:09,983 --> 00:51:12,569
You can't lose control!

794
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:15,405
That came out wrong.
I meant, don't act crazy.

795
00:51:16,615 --> 00:51:19,618
- What, are you dying?
- Not yet, at least.

796
00:51:21,203 --> 00:51:25,665
Huh! Hey, Ayane! Spending your free time
with the boyfriend?

797
00:51:27,334 --> 00:51:28,418
I guess so.

798
00:51:35,425 --> 00:51:37,344
Kento! C'mon, let's go.

799
00:51:37,886 --> 00:51:38,720
'Kay!

800
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:49,648
There's more distance.

801
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:53,735
Did I... cause it without realizing?

802
00:51:54,820 --> 00:51:57,948
There's our two lovebirds!

803
00:51:58,031 --> 00:51:59,741
- Hi!
- Takahashi!

804
00:51:59,825 --> 00:52:04,287
Mmmm? Ahhhh! Uhhh?

805
00:52:05,330 --> 00:52:06,164
Heh.

806
00:52:06,748 --> 00:52:08,625
Oh no, this just won't do.

807
00:52:08,708 --> 00:52:10,919
Both of you are so nervous
and on edge today.

808
00:52:12,462 --> 00:52:15,507
Have you two taken any pictures
or anything together?

809
00:52:15,590 --> 00:52:18,009
N-- no, we haven't taken any yet.

810
00:52:18,093 --> 00:52:19,886
There's a super cute spot over there

811
00:52:19,970 --> 00:52:22,472
that's perfect for couples
to take photos together.

812
00:52:22,556 --> 00:52:23,890
I could take some for you!

813
00:52:24,474 --> 00:52:26,893
Oh, uh... thank you,
but you don't have to do all that.

814
00:52:26,977 --> 00:52:28,770
C'mon?! What are you talking about?

815
00:52:28,854 --> 00:52:29,688
Tell me.

816
00:52:29,771 --> 00:52:33,775
Does that mean you don't care at all
about making Sadako happy as your partner?

817
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:35,819
I-- I'm already really happy, so...

818
00:52:38,989 --> 00:52:41,575
Kuronuma, let's take some pictures!

819
00:52:42,450 --> 00:52:45,162
Look at that,
he wants to make the girl he loves happy!

820
00:52:45,245 --> 00:52:46,746
Yay! What a man.

821
00:52:46,830 --> 00:52:49,583
You're gonna need to stop talking
like that. Seriously.

822
00:52:52,294 --> 00:52:53,503
Mmmm!

823
00:52:53,587 --> 00:52:57,299
Mmm! Oh wow!
You've got a really nice camera.

824
00:52:57,382 --> 00:52:59,593
Just take the picture. Please.

825
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:02,262
Huh? What?
I didn't know those two were together!

826
00:53:02,345 --> 00:53:04,598
Sorry, something just came up.

827
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:06,391
Perfect timing!

828
00:53:06,474 --> 00:53:08,268
- Could you take over?
- Huh?

829
00:53:09,269 --> 00:53:10,312
Hmm.

830
00:53:16,401 --> 00:53:19,362
I'm gonna take a photo of the prince
of Kitahoro High School

831
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,573
and the happiest moment
of his entire life!

832
00:53:21,656 --> 00:53:23,325
Why are you like this?!

833
00:53:23,408 --> 00:53:25,827
POTTERY STREET

834
00:53:25,911 --> 00:53:29,289
- These shisa are adorable.
- I think I like those ones more.

835
00:53:29,372 --> 00:53:32,417
Huh?
The ones on the left are way cuter!

836
00:53:34,419 --> 00:53:36,254
- So, hey...
- Huh?

837
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:38,548
- Huh?
- It's Mogi!

838
00:53:39,049 --> 00:53:40,967
Hey! Over here!

839
00:53:41,676 --> 00:53:43,011
Uh...

840
00:53:43,094 --> 00:53:45,138
Don't worry about me, you go ahead.

841
00:53:45,222 --> 00:53:48,600
I'll do some browsing around here.
I've been wanting to shop anyway.

842
00:53:49,100 --> 00:53:50,644
Oh... if you're sure.

843
00:53:51,144 --> 00:53:51,978
Later!

844
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:55,565
What's goin' on?
Have you been hangin' around here?

845
00:53:57,108 --> 00:53:57,943
Hmm.

846
00:54:07,285 --> 00:54:08,703
Wow! This is a pig?!

847
00:54:09,412 --> 00:54:10,622
The fish are amazing!

848
00:54:10,705 --> 00:54:14,251
- Everything's amazing!
- Joe is always so fricking annoying!

849
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:16,962
But, I'm actually glad he's here.

850
00:54:18,713 --> 00:54:21,258
I didn't think you were gonna come.

851
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:25,679
Huh? Just because I didn't want to make
Yano-chin and Sawako change their plans!

852
00:54:25,762 --> 00:54:27,055
So don't be dumb! Ugh!

853
00:54:27,138 --> 00:54:30,225
Me being here has nothing to do
with you, okay? It's all for my girlies!

854
00:54:31,393 --> 00:54:32,686
Mm-hmm.

855
00:54:32,769 --> 00:54:33,853
But still,

856
00:54:34,396 --> 00:54:37,941
being alone together probably isn't
what either of us wants right now.

857
00:54:38,024 --> 00:54:41,319
At least, that's how I feel.
And Ryu's probably the same.

858
00:54:42,487 --> 00:54:44,030
- Chizuru.
- Mmm?

859
00:54:44,906 --> 00:54:45,740
Ice cream.

860
00:54:46,574 --> 00:54:47,492
Uh?

861
00:54:48,201 --> 00:54:49,119
You owe me.

862
00:54:51,079 --> 00:54:54,582
HANDMADE ITALIAN GELATO

863
00:54:54,666 --> 00:54:56,418
Yum! Yum!

864
00:54:57,836 --> 00:55:00,088
What is happening?!

865
00:55:00,588 --> 00:55:01,423
So good.

866
00:55:01,506 --> 00:55:04,843
How are you able to get me
to buy you ice cream at a time like this?

867
00:55:04,926 --> 00:55:06,303
Well, you promised me.

868
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:07,721
What the-- Not!

869
00:55:07,804 --> 00:55:11,766
Oh, that's not fair! How come you didn't
buy ice cream for me too, Yoshida?

870
00:55:11,850 --> 00:55:14,686
Why would you ever think
I was supposed to buy you ice cream?

871
00:55:14,769 --> 00:55:17,897
It doesn't make any sense,
no matter how I think about it!

872
00:55:19,190 --> 00:55:20,275
Oh, hey, Ryu.

873
00:55:20,358 --> 00:55:23,320
So why'd you end up
turning down that girl from Class C?

874
00:55:23,403 --> 00:55:25,905
Is there somebody else that you like?

875
00:55:26,823 --> 00:55:30,035
- Hmm.
- No way, really? Who is it, who?!

876
00:55:30,118 --> 00:55:31,745
It's none of your business, Joe.

877
00:55:31,828 --> 00:55:34,247
- What's your deal?! Just tell me, c'mon!
- Yep.

878
00:55:34,331 --> 00:55:36,166
- And it's none of my business either.
- No.

879
00:55:36,249 --> 00:55:37,500
Okay, but why?!

880
00:55:38,835 --> 00:55:41,755
That's right.
It's none of my business.

881
00:55:42,339 --> 00:55:44,049
And he won't tell me anyway.

882
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:52,557
I thought... I knew everything
there was to know about Ryu.

883
00:55:53,350 --> 00:55:54,476
But he likes someone.

884
00:55:55,185 --> 00:55:59,689
And I had to hear that for the first time
from a girl I barely even know.

885
00:56:00,982 --> 00:56:02,192
But why?

886
00:56:02,901 --> 00:56:04,402
He knows that I like Toru,

887
00:56:04,486 --> 00:56:07,530
so why can't he tell me who he likes.

888
00:56:09,032 --> 00:56:13,244
I guess it's different.
Ryu found out who I like on his own.

889
00:56:13,328 --> 00:56:15,455
I'm not the one who told him.

890
00:56:15,538 --> 00:56:20,710
But... I guess childhood friends
are just like this.

891
00:56:20,794 --> 00:56:22,045
But still...

892
00:56:23,129 --> 00:56:23,963
Still...

893
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:27,717
I was wondering
how you felt about Sanada?

894
00:56:27,801 --> 00:56:30,261
If you don't like Sanada,
I wanted to let him know

895
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:32,514
he shouldn't hang out with you so much.

896
00:56:32,597 --> 00:56:36,643
That's none of your business!
You have no right to say anything!

897
00:56:37,644 --> 00:56:39,646
The two of us have always...

898
00:56:41,648 --> 00:56:43,650
But... am I right?

899
00:56:44,359 --> 00:56:46,694
Maybe I'm the only one
who thinks that way.

900
00:56:47,612 --> 00:56:50,156
Maybe it's really just
none of my business.

901
00:56:50,824 --> 00:56:53,284
Maybe I don't deserve to feel this

902
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:55,161
angry at Ryu.

903
00:56:57,080 --> 00:57:00,667
Maybe this entire time,
he's had someone he's liked,

904
00:57:00,750 --> 00:57:02,252
and I just didn't know.

905
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:04,963
One day,

906
00:57:06,005 --> 00:57:08,049
is he going to start dating someone?

907
00:57:10,552 --> 00:57:12,387
This baseball idiot?

908
00:57:13,847 --> 00:57:16,224
Okay! I'm gonna go get seconds!

909
00:57:16,307 --> 00:57:20,311
Oh wow! So what do we have here?
Ooo, and what's this one? Mmm!

910
00:57:20,395 --> 00:57:23,440
Oh, hey! What a coincidence!
What are you guys up to?

911
00:57:23,523 --> 00:57:25,066
- Whoa!
- It's Joe!

912
00:57:26,109 --> 00:57:28,736
So, this is probably
not gonna end well, right?

913
00:57:28,820 --> 00:57:31,072
- Maybe it's fate?
- C'mon!

914
00:57:35,160 --> 00:57:37,287
- This is good.
- Mmm.

915
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:45,378
This one's good too.

916
00:57:46,129 --> 00:57:47,088
Damn right.

917
00:57:51,885 --> 00:57:53,887
Don't you feel a little awkward?

918
00:57:56,389 --> 00:57:58,266
When I got upset at you yesterday,

919
00:57:58,349 --> 00:58:00,143
do you have any idea why?

920
00:58:04,647 --> 00:58:07,484
- Are you listening?
- Yeah.

921
00:58:11,946 --> 00:58:13,573
It made me happy...

922
00:58:16,034 --> 00:58:16,868
...that you cared.

923
00:58:17,744 --> 00:58:21,456
That you were at least
a little interested in... who I might like.

924
00:58:22,582 --> 00:58:23,708
It made me happy.

925
00:58:26,794 --> 00:58:28,129
Since that person

926
00:58:29,339 --> 00:58:30,590
was always you.

927
00:58:36,888 --> 00:58:38,890
Thank you for shopping with us!

928
00:58:41,017 --> 00:58:42,810
Where did everyone go?

929
00:58:43,603 --> 00:58:46,814
Are you serious?
C'mon, I was so sure!

930
00:58:46,898 --> 00:58:50,151
You went from dating to kissing,
just like that, ya know?

931
00:58:50,235 --> 00:58:52,737
I thought everything
was moving along quick and easy.

932
00:58:52,820 --> 00:58:54,113
We're talkin' about Yano.

933
00:58:54,197 --> 00:58:55,740
Yeah, maybe you're right.

934
00:58:55,823 --> 00:58:58,451
I guess I just set
my expectations too high is all.

935
00:58:58,535 --> 00:59:00,286
- What about today?
- No way.

936
00:59:00,370 --> 00:59:03,289
- We haven't even held hands yet today.
- Is this what you want?

937
00:59:03,373 --> 00:59:04,374
Uh?

938
00:59:04,958 --> 00:59:06,417
H-- hi, Yano!

939
00:59:06,501 --> 00:59:08,878
What's going on?
So it's like that?

940
00:59:08,962 --> 00:59:11,506
Are you kidding me? Gimme a break!

941
00:59:11,589 --> 00:59:13,383
I actually thought
you were a trustworthy guy.

942
00:59:13,466 --> 00:59:16,553
I know what
you're thinking, but Mogi isn't a bad guy.

943
00:59:16,636 --> 00:59:18,596
Nah, I think you just got the wrong idea!

944
00:59:18,680 --> 00:59:22,016
For sure! It's just that
he got his hopes up about you, y'know?

945
00:59:22,684 --> 00:59:26,229
And got disappointed without ever asking
if I'm comfortable doing things like that?

946
00:59:26,312 --> 00:59:28,523
- That's skeevy.
- You're right!

947
00:59:28,606 --> 00:59:30,400
Uh...

948
00:59:30,483 --> 00:59:31,568
Y-- Yano.

949
00:59:32,652 --> 00:59:33,736
I'm so sorry.

950
00:59:37,448 --> 00:59:38,491
It's okay.

951
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:42,787
But... I don't feel like
continuing this relationship anymore.

952
00:59:42,870 --> 00:59:43,871
I understand.

953
00:59:45,456 --> 00:59:46,374
See ya.

954
00:59:48,668 --> 00:59:49,919
Uh... Yano!

955
00:59:50,753 --> 00:59:53,047
For real, I am sorry.

956
00:59:53,756 --> 00:59:56,259
Were you trying to
tell me something before?

957
01:00:00,847 --> 01:00:03,141
Sorry, about yesterday.

958
01:00:09,522 --> 01:00:10,356
Nope.

959
01:00:11,357 --> 01:00:14,777
- That's so cute!
- I wanna take it home!

960
01:00:15,778 --> 01:00:18,865
Hey, you've gotta stop them
before they really get outta hand.

961
01:00:20,074 --> 01:00:22,994
Huh?

962
01:00:27,332 --> 01:00:29,292
Huh? Hey, Kento.

963
01:00:30,084 --> 01:00:32,045
I've gotta go. Sorry.

964
01:00:32,128 --> 01:00:33,713
Huh? Where are you going?!

965
01:00:37,091 --> 01:00:38,009
Ayane!

966
01:00:40,011 --> 01:00:40,845
What's wrong?

967
01:00:41,554 --> 01:00:42,388
Kento.

968
01:00:42,889 --> 01:00:44,390
What are you doing here alone?

969
01:00:45,099 --> 01:00:46,267
Where's Mogi-cchi?

970
01:00:47,226 --> 01:00:49,228
We just broke up.

971
01:00:50,271 --> 01:00:51,564
What happened?

972
01:00:54,609 --> 01:00:56,694
Now that I think about it,
no wonder.

973
01:00:57,945 --> 01:01:00,490
What things
do the two of you talk about?

974
01:01:00,573 --> 01:01:02,325
In conversations,

975
01:01:02,408 --> 01:01:05,411
he'd always just go along
with whatever I was talking about.

976
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:07,705
There was never any substance.

977
01:01:08,790 --> 01:01:12,502
And the day we started dating,
he didn't even walk home with me.

978
01:01:13,711 --> 01:01:17,548
I bet after that, he went straight
to report it to his friends.

979
01:01:17,632 --> 01:01:18,966
He never...

980
01:01:19,050 --> 01:01:21,344
he never actually liked me at all.

981
01:01:21,844 --> 01:01:23,179
I'm fine.

982
01:01:24,055 --> 01:01:25,473
I really am okay.

983
01:01:26,766 --> 01:01:27,975
Nothing's wrong.

984
01:01:30,645 --> 01:01:32,063
Even though we kissed...

985
01:01:32,855 --> 01:01:34,732
I-- I was wondering,

986
01:01:34,816 --> 01:01:37,402
when did you
first start having feelings for Mogi?

987
01:01:37,485 --> 01:01:40,655
You've got it all wrong, Sawako.
We aren't the same.

988
01:01:42,323 --> 01:01:44,158
It's not like it is for you.

989
01:01:44,242 --> 01:01:46,953
Where anyone could tell
how much your heart was racing

990
01:01:47,036 --> 01:01:48,579
with just a quick glance.

991
01:01:49,747 --> 01:01:51,958
Because I never liked him at all.

992
01:01:57,672 --> 01:02:01,551
Kento, you've had a lot of girlfriends
until now, haven't you?

993
01:02:01,634 --> 01:02:03,970
You... you make it sound
like it's a bad thing.

994
01:02:04,470 --> 01:02:06,764
But have you ever
fallen in love with someone?

995
01:02:09,058 --> 01:02:09,976
Have I...

996
01:02:10,059 --> 01:02:12,937
Well, of course,
that's why I started dating them.

997
01:02:14,689 --> 01:02:15,606
I haven't.

998
01:02:17,191 --> 01:02:19,110
I've never fallen in love with anyone.

999
01:02:19,944 --> 01:02:23,114
I've never dated someone
because I like them.

1000
01:02:24,157 --> 01:02:26,117
That's why... I can't...

1001
01:02:27,326 --> 01:02:28,453
Ayane, hey.

1002
01:02:29,370 --> 01:02:31,748
I can't be like Sawako and Chizu.

1003
01:02:33,249 --> 01:02:35,293
It's... just that

1004
01:02:36,836 --> 01:02:40,673
when I see people pour their hearts out
or be on the receiving end,

1005
01:02:42,717 --> 01:02:45,178
it gives me hope that I could be the same.

1006
01:02:45,845 --> 01:02:47,180
I thought maybe

1007
01:02:47,263 --> 01:02:50,641
he was showing that kind of vulnerability
with me when he confessed.

1008
01:02:52,059 --> 01:02:55,146
And that maybe
I could come to love him in time.

1009
01:02:56,814 --> 01:02:58,941
That's what I thought.

1010
01:03:04,614 --> 01:03:07,200
Don't get me wrong. I don't...

1011
01:03:07,742 --> 01:03:11,120
I don't feel sad
or anything like that.

1012
01:03:22,298 --> 01:03:24,217
I said it's not like that.

1013
01:03:28,596 --> 01:03:31,349
How come... you're not saying anything?

1014
01:03:47,281 --> 01:03:49,408
All right! Everyone here?

1015
01:03:50,076 --> 01:03:52,203
Time for us to fly back to Hokkaido!

1016
01:03:52,286 --> 01:03:54,580
Let's hurry up and get home already!

1017
01:03:54,664 --> 01:03:56,624
Huh? What's goin' on
with you, Pin?

1018
01:03:56,707 --> 01:03:58,626
Yesterday, you said
you were never goin' home.

1019
01:03:58,709 --> 01:04:02,338
I heard he asked Higa
for a long-distance relationship,

1020
01:04:02,421 --> 01:04:03,631
and she turned him down.

1021
01:04:03,714 --> 01:04:04,549
Really?

1022
01:04:05,758 --> 01:04:07,969
Do you think
it's gonna be cold when we get back?

1023
01:04:08,052 --> 01:04:10,888
- I hope not.
- You're always cold, Yano-chin.

1024
01:04:10,972 --> 01:04:13,349
Well, I don't like being too hot either.

1025
01:04:13,432 --> 01:04:15,893
You just need to learn
how to deal with being uncomfy.

1026
01:04:20,314 --> 01:04:23,901
Since that person... was always you.

1027
01:04:25,486 --> 01:04:27,905
There's never been anyone else.

1028
01:04:31,075 --> 01:04:32,034
Ryu, I've...

1029
01:04:33,828 --> 01:04:35,538
never thought of you like that.

1030
01:04:36,998 --> 01:04:37,874
Yeah.

1031
01:04:39,166 --> 01:04:40,126
I know.

1032
01:04:44,463 --> 01:04:48,342
For all of us...
it's the start of a new season.
